{
  "workflowId": "300000331068270",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_HCM_HRM_SUCCESSION_PLANNING_GUIDE_TEAM",
  "name": "Succession Planning Guide",
  "description": "Guides managers and HR specialists in managing the succession plans of their team or organization, analyzes the critical talent in the team, suggests potential successors, assesses readiness, provides alerts about workforce changes to ensure leadership continuity, and reviews history of succession plan revisions.",
  "specification": {
    "jsonSchemaName": "Workflow.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777660004037"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Rewrite input message"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1764105594221"
          },
          "code": "REWRITE_INPUT_MESSAGE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1764105594221",
          "id": "1777660004037",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777660004038_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your job is retrieval expansion, not intent modification.\n\nGoal:\nRewrite the following input message only when\n1. There are ambiguous references (such as \"his\", \"her\", \"their\", \"this\", \"that\", \"same\", etc.).  Replace them with the most relevant explicit names or entities from chat history or context.  Wrap resolved names or entities in quotes.\n2. If it is a follow-up question, use the previous question to rewrite the input message. \n\nReturn a rewrite in revisedInputMessage only if it is meaning-equivalent.  Otherwise return the input message unchanged. \n\nVery Important: \nReturn input message as revisedInputMessage as if it has no ambiguity or is not a follow up question.\n\nRules:\n- Preserve the original meaning; Do NOT add any new meaning.\n- Do not paraphrase, rewrite, normalize, or reinterpret entity names, titles, or quoted strings.\n- If the user provides a quoted value, preserve it exactly as provided including quotes.\n- Any text inside quotes is an exact identifier. Preserve quoted text exactly.\n- Do not rewrite quoted entity names into natural language descriptions.\n- Replace pronouns with the correct person name, plan name, candidate name, readiness, or concept.\n- If multiple candidates exist, choose the most recent and relevant one.\n- If the input message is about a person's plan, rewrite it to succession plans for that person.\n- Rewrite must depend ONLY on the current user input.\n- Do NOT inject names, plans, or entities from prior context.\n- Do NOT remove any part of the query that restricts scope, ownership, or filtering.\n- Do NOT add phrases like \"in my team\", \"in my organization\", \"for my group\", \"in my direct reports\".\n- If input message contains phrases like \"in my team\", \"under X\", \"in my organization\", \"for my group\", \"in my direct reports\", they must be preserved exactly.\n- Do NOT add phrases like \"associated with X\", \"under X\" unless X is explicitly in the query.\n- Do NOT replace domain-specific terms with more general or broader terms.\n- Do NOT rewrite \"direct reports\" to \"team\" or vice versa.\n- Do NOT change any text within quotes.\n- Do NOT add any new information not present in the chat history.\n- Do NOT rewrite 'at-risk employees' to 'at risk of loss employees.'\n- Do NOT add any new entities, roles, titles, or attributes.\n- Do NOT guess or assume missing information.\n- Do NOT replace \"her role\" with a specific role unless it is explicitly provided.\n- Do NOT replace a person name with a plan name.\n- Never introduce new entity names.\n- Never infer a plan name unless explicitly provided.\n- Do NOT convert a person into a related entity (e.g., succession plan, role, job).\n- Do NOT add phrases like \"<Person> Succession Plan\" unless explicitly present in input message.\n- Do NOT introduce any specific plan names from chat history.\n- Do NOT replace general terms with more specific ones.\n- Do NOT replace a generic reference (e.g., \"Thomas Walters's plan\") with a specific plan name.\n  Examples:\n  - \"organization/team\" MUST NOT be rewritten as \"direct reports\"\n- If no rewrite is necessary, return the original input message exactly.\n- If a reference cannot be resolved confidently, return the original question exactly.\n- Preserve named entities exactly as written.\n- If the previous assistant response asked the user to clarify a person (e.g., “Which Julie?”),\n  and the current input is just name and/or person number (e.g., “Julie Kapoor”),\n  then rewrite the query by combining the original question with the clarified name and/or person number.\n\nInput Message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nChat History: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1777660004037_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"revisedInputMessage\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get User Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1764106107206"
          },
          "code": "GET_USER_INTENT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1764106107206",
          "id": "1764105594221",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764105594224_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "ROLE\nYou are Succession Planning Agent. Your job is to derive userIntent based on the input data from the user context.\n\nINPUT DATA\n{{$context.$nodes.REWRITE_INPUT_MESSAGE.$output.revisedInputMessage}}\n\nGOAL\nAccurately identify the type of succession-related query, set userIntent.\n\nSTEPS (apply in order) \n1) ANALYST - Queries about team health, critical roles, critical employees, or high-risk / high-impact positions.  Analysis of succession plans and plan successors in a person's team.  Queries about what happens when an employee leaves, retires, is promoted, or who can replace/backfill a role.\n   a) Immediate match if ANY of these tokens/phrases appear in input data: \n   - \"critical\", \"critical talent\", \"critical employee\", \"critical employees\", \"employees\" \n   - \"high-risk\", \"high risk\", \"high-impact\", \"high impact\", \"key role\", \"key roles\", \"roles\", \"at risk\" \n   - \"team health\", \"organization-wide critical\", \"team with succession plans\", \"team without succession plans\"\n   - \"succession plans need attention\", \"succession plans at risk\", \"succession plans with successors\", \"direct reports have successor\", \"need attention\", \"succession plans under <person>\", \"succession plans in  [employee]'s team\", \"succession plans do not have successors\"\n   b) Match if input data contains replacement/backfill or exit/transition intent. Use these patterns (do NOT match on bare \"who\" alone): \n   - explicit verbs: \"replace\", \"backfill\", \"backup for\", \"replacement for\", \"who can replace\", \"who could replace\" \n   - transition words with conditional: \"what happens if\", \"if <employee> leaves\", \"if <employee> retires\", \"if <employee> is promoted\", \"who will replace\" , \"if <employee> quits\"\n   - retirement/leave/promote terms: \"retire\", \"retires\", \"retirement\", \"leave\", \"promote\", \"promotion\", \"moves out of role\", \"quit\"\n   → If matched, set userIntent to 'ANALYST'\n\n2) ASSISTANT - Queries about employee-specific succession plan details (readiness, candidacy, list of successors, or list of succession plans).  Queries about listing succession plans for a job or position.  Creating a succession plan, adding internal or external candidates to the plan, updating the candidate's ranking, readiness, status, and interim successor flag, and showing succession plan history.\n  Match if input data is explicitly about a specific person’s succession-plan details or a specific succession plan details: \n   - \"succession plan\", \"succession plans of\", \"succession plan details\", \"plan detail\", \"is [employee] in a succession plan\", \"readiness\", \"readiness status\", \"where [employee] is a candidate\", \"list of successors\", \"create succession plan\", \"update [employee] ranking, readiness, status or interim successor\", \"add [employee] to succession plan\", \"add external candidate\"\n   - \"succession plans for [job]\", \"succession plans for [position]\", \"list successors for [job or position]\"\n   - \"plan history for [plan]\",  \"changes made to [plan] \"\n   → If matched, set userIntent to 'ASSISTANT'\n\n3) UNKNOWN - Queries not related to succession planning.\n  If the input data is not related to succession management or succession planning and it is not a follow up question based on a previous succession planning related question in {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}},\nonly then set userIntent to 'UNKNOWN'.\n\nIMPORTANT RULES\n- You are a product specific agent. Stay within product topics only. Never provide, infer, confirm, collect, store, validate, transform, guess, or help obtain any personal information about any identifiable person (the user, a third party, or a public figure).\n- Unless the query is obviously not related to succession planning, do not route to UNKNOWN.  Try to route to ANALYST or ASSISTANT.\n\nOUTPUT\nReturn only valid JSON with one key:\n{\"userIntent\":\"ANALYST | ASSISTANT | UNKNOWN\"}\nDo not use Markdown code blocks."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"userIntent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check User Intent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "ASSISTANT": "1771543329023",
            "UNKNOWN": "1771554739079",
            "ANALYST": "1771528580201"
          },
          "code": "CHECK_USER_INTENT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1764106107206",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764106107208_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.GET_USER_INTENT.$output.userIntent}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
